  CVE-2026-40685|2026-04-30T22:16:25.633|2026-05-01T17:51:06.830|6.5|MEDIUM|CWE-684|N/A|false|In Exim before 4.99.2, when JSON lookup is enabled, an out-of-bounds heap write can occur when a JSON operator encounters malformed JSON in an untrusted header, because of an incorrect implementation of \ skipping.|https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-40685|0.00054|0.16622|4.5516
  CVE-2026-40684|2026-04-30T22:16:25.477|2026-05-01T18:16:15.343|5.9|MEDIUM|CWE-684|N/A|false|In Exim before 4.99.2, on systems using musl libc (not glibc), an attacker can crash the connection instance when malformed DNS data is present in PTR records. This is caused by a dn_expand oddity in octal printing.|https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-40684|0.00055|0.16903|4.1316
  CVE-2026-3345|2026-04-30T22:16:25.337|2026-05-01T15:27:15.287|6.5|MEDIUM|CWE-22|N/A|false|"IBM Langflow Desktop <=1.8.4 Langflow could allow a remote attacker to traverse directories on the system. An attacker could send a specially crafted URL request containing ""dot dot"" sequences (/../) to view arbitrary files on the system."|https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-3345|0.00052|0.16169|4.5516
