  CVE-2026-5756|2026-04-14T18:17:39.600|2026-04-23T14:16:04.840|7.5|HIGH|N/A|N/A|false|Unauthenticated Configuration File Modification Vulnerability in DRC Central Office Services (COS) allows an attacker to modify the server's configuration file, potentially leading to mass data exfiltration, malicious traffic interception, or disruption of testing services.|https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-5756|0.00039|0.11500|5.2512
