  CVE-2026-34617|2026-04-14T18:17:36.540|2026-04-22T19:36:51.940|8.7|HIGH|CWE-79|N/A|false|Adobe Connect versions 2025.3, 12.10 and earlier are affected by a Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) vulnerability that could result in privilege escalation. A low-privileged attacker could exploit this vulnerability to inject malicious scripts into a web page, potentially gaining elevated access or control over the victim's account or session. Exploitation of this issue requires user interaction in that a victim must visit a maliciously crafted URL or interact with a compromised web page. Scope is changed.|https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-34617|0.00043|0.12972|6.0913
