  CVE-2026-6137|2026-04-13T00:16:21.300|2026-04-30T12:35:12.503|7.4|HIGH|CWE-119|N/A|false|A vulnerability was detected in Tenda F451 1.0.0.7_cn_svn7958. The affected element is the function fromAdvSetWan of the file /goform/AdvSetWan. The manipulation of the argument wanmode/PPPOEPassword results in stack-based buffer overflow. It is possible to launch the attack remotely. The exploit is now public and may be used.|https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-6137|0.00081|0.23683|5.1824
